    26	 *  frozen due; a claim already bound keeps the due it was bound to): while bound, its late charge no longer follows the
    27	 *  sheet's today; a claim with no figure because the rate that would apply to it has ended is bound to n/a; a
    28	 *  claim that does not count is unbound (live again). The due-total is as shown: the sum of the counting claims' dues now (late charges
    29	 *  included), skipping those with none; 'n/a' when no rate for the grade they have on the sheet's today
    30	 *  is in force then and no counting claim has a fixed figure or a due (at the grade it was claimed under); at
    31	 *  most the sheet's cap.
