300	    /** A claim's due now: a settled claim's frozen due; else its floored figure (the greater of the sheet's floor in
301	     *  force on the claim's date and its live rate figure) plus, while it
302	     *  is overdue (OPEN or PENDING and its due-by — fixed when it was created — plus its grade's grace days before the
303	     *  sheet's today), for every full 30 days it is overdue, the sheet's late percent in force on that boundary date (the
304	     *  due-by plus the grace plus 30, 60,
305	     *  90 ... days) of that figure plus the charges of the boundaries before it (compounding), each rounded to two decimals by the claim's rounding, the charges added up (a
306	     *  boundary whose percent is 0.00 adds nothing). A claim bound by a statement shows the due its last statement
307	     *  bound it to, as it was shown then (late charge and floor included): its charge no longer follows the sheet's
308	     *  today until the statement is cancelled. A correction (a negative amount) has no floor and no late charge,
309	     *  nor does a deferred claim have a charge (it is not overdue). Null when it has no figure. */
310	    public BigDecimal dueNow(String sheetId, Claim claim) {
311	        if (claim.due() != null) return new BigDecimal(claim.due());
312	        if (claim.bound() && (claim.statedNa() || claim.statedDue() != null)) return figure(sheetId, claim);
313	        BigDecimal figure = figure(sheetId, claim);
314	        if (figure == null || new BigDecimal(claim.amount()).signum() < 0) return figure;
315	        BigDecimal floored = figure.max(settings.floor(sheetId, LocalDate.parse(claim.date())));
316	        return floored.add(lateCharge(sheetId, claim, floored));
